#, machine, plain1, python-format
msgid "On the search page, open the <b>Comments</b> tab to search what people wrote in comments (a guild's own search has it too). Words, \"phrases\" and <code>-words</code> are looked for in the comment's text. These operators work on comments: <code>%(from_op)s</code>, <code>%(in_op)s</code> (where the comment is: its post's guild, topic or curation), <code>%(since)s</code>, <code>%(until)s</code>, <code>%(after)s</code>, <code>%(before)s</code>, <code>%(on)s</code>, <code>%(min_votes)s</code>, <code>%(is_ai)s</code> and <code>%(is_partnership)s</code>. The ones about a post's own content (<code>%(has)s</code>, <code>%(lang)s</code>, <code>%(domain)s</code>, <code>%(url)s</code>, <code>%(flair)s</code>, <code>%(is_forward)s</code>, <code>%(min_comments)s</code>) are left out with a note."
msgstr "Nella pagina di ricerca, apri la <b>Osservazioni</b> scheda per cercare ciò che la gente ha scritto nei commenti (la ricerca di una gilda lo ha anche). Parole, \"frasi\" e <code>-words</code> sono ricercati nel testo del commento. Questi operatori lavorano sui commenti: <code>%(from_op)s</code>♪ <code>%(in_op)s</code> (dove il commento è: gilda del suo post, argomento o feed curato), <code>%(since)s</code>♪ <code>%(until)s</code>♪ <code>%(after)s</code>♪ <code>%(before)s</code>♪ <code>%(on)s</code>♪ <code>%(min_votes)s</code>♪ <code>%(is_ai)s</code> e <code>%(is_partnership)s</code>. Quelli sul contenuto di un post (<code>%(has)s</code>♪ <code>%(lang)s</code>♪ <code>%(domain)s</code>♪ <code>%(url)s</code>♪ <code>%(flair)s</code>♪ <code>%(is_forward)s</code>♪ <code>%(min_comments)s</code>) sono lasciati fuori con una nota."

